## Overview

This room introduces the **AWS Shared Responsibility Model** and explains how security responsibilities are divided between AWS and its customers.

AWS is responsible for securing the underlying cloud infrastructure (**Security OF the Cloud**), while customers are responsible for securing the services, identities, applications, and data they configure and deploy (**Security IN the Cloud**). The exact division of responsibility depends on the cloud service model being used.

The room also examines real-world cloud security incidents to demonstrate how exposed credentials, overly permissive IAM policies, and misconfigured storage can lead to severe data exposure.

